p.src:
There is a second and equally important piece of arithmetic. The lecture is really about contract control: $L_{\mathrm{control}}
=
\frac{V_{\mathrm{contract}}}{E_{\mathrm{earnest+option}}}
\approx
\frac{2{,}000{,}000}{20{,}000}
=100.$ This is not presented as debt leverage. It is contract-control leverage: a relatively small outlay secures control over a much larger commercial path.

